The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) calls the ticket one issue with one fix queued. Its own
table says otherwise, and the reports say more. Read the bodies, not the subject lines, and the
ticket holds three problems. Each one now has a ticket of its own.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. The parser fix that is queued closes only the first row below. The other two stay
open after it ships.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant on file writes
  the day first. Day and month swap: 7 April goes out as 4 July. Reports by app, by email, and
  by the `booking-v2` form, whose hint says `DD/MM/YYYY`.
- **`hint`**: the `booking-v3` form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type month
  first, as told, and the form reads it day first. Same symptom, different place: a parser fix
  does not touch it.
- **`shift`**: no swap at all. The date moves by one day ("Tuesday 6 October showed as Monday"),
  or the invite arrives before the booking, or two attendees in two time zones get two different
  days. The desk had read these as one-day moves (`desk-notes.json`) and still counted them
  under the parser.

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports whose subject lines match,
without reading the body. Every one of these reports says "wrong day" in some form, so all three
problems landed in one ticket. The subject tells you that a date is wrong, not why. Intake's tag
does not help either: it is guessed from the reporter's browser, and the table counts how often
it disagrees with the tenant.

The table the #4471 page shows, for comparison. It places reports by tenant and channel only, so
the one-day moves sit under `parser`:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## For the desk

- Before merging into a big ticket, read a sample of bodies. A swap (4 July for 7 April) and a
  one-day move (Monday for Tuesday) are different bugs with the same subject line.
- Place a report by its tenant (locale and booking form), not by intake's tag.
- Decision 0001 needs a successor record: subject match proposes a merge, a person confirms it.

